		"TECH_BRANCH_MILITARY_DESC": "Morale: your people recover faster when everything is paid. A colony that knows it is defended holds up better.",
		"TECH_BRANCH_LOGISTICS_DESC": "Market, storage and build speed. Roads and depots the Empire knows nothing about.",
		"TECH_LORE_ind_1": "Imperial factory manuals, copied by hand from one they think was burnt.",
		"TECH_LORE_ind_2": "Stores that appear on no map. What they cannot see, they cannot collect.",
		"TECH_LORE_ind_3": "Double shifts and boilers at full pressure. The Regency would call it yield; here we call it eating.",
		"TECH_LORE_ind_4": "Rations weighed to the gram. We learned to keep the books, and now we keep them ourselves.",
		"TECH_LORE_ind_5": "Machines that never tire or break. What the Empire denied us, rebuilt from scrap.",
		"TECH_LORE_mil_1": "Falling in without uniform or flag. A forgotten people can still take roll call.",
		"TECH_LORE_mil_2": "Drill with scrap rifles. The Collectors bring an escort; so do we.",
		"TECH_LORE_mil_3": "Studying the Collectors: where they come in, what they look at first, how long they stay.",
		"TECH_LORE_mil_4": "Sandbags and riveted plate. A colony that defends itself is not so easy to collect from.",
		"TECH_LORE_mil_5": "We no longer ask not to be collected. We decide who comes in.",
		"TECH_LORE_log_1": "Smugglers who know the gaps in the blockade. At the Market, those who know the way in pay less.",
