		"TUT_TIP_BARRACKS_TITLE": "The Barracks",
		"TUT_TIP_BARRACKS_BODY": "Trains soldiers. In era 1, Infantry; Artillery comes with steel (Foundry) and the Tank with oil (Refinery). Each barracks trains one at a time and you pay up front: ☰ MENU > COLONY > ARMY.\n\nWhy early: after every Storm the Tax Collectors come down, and only your troops at home fight so they take nothing. The first one, around minute 5, is a practice run. From MISSIONS your soldiers go out for loot.",
		"TUT_TIP_MARKET_TITLE": "The Market",
		"TUT_TIP_MARKET_BODY": "Buy and sell against gold. Buying pushes the price up and selling pushes it down; over time it drifts back. You always buy dearer than you sell: use it to plug a gap, not to live off it.",
		"TUT_TIP_TECH_TITLE": "The tech tree",
		"TUT_TIP_TECH_BODY": "It is researched at the Laboratory: tap it on the map. It grants permanent advantages: Industrial raises production (+10% already at tier 1) and storage, Military recovers morale faster and Transport makes the Market cheaper and speeds up construction. Each tech states its advantage in numbers.\n\nIt costs resources and time, one at a time, and each branch goes in order: tier 2 needs tier 1. If one is greyed out, the reason is written under it.",
		"TUT_TIP_MAP_TITLE": "The expedition map",
		"TUT_TIP_MAP_BODY": "You go left to right, one stop at a time. The number with the soldier is how many enemies; the risk is written below: more risk, more enemies and more loot. Wounds do not heal between stops. You can abandon and keep the loot; the boss waits at the end.",
		"TUT_TIP_UPKEEP_TITLE": "Paying the troops",
		"TUT_TIP_UPKEEP_BODY": "Every unit is paid in gold every minute and a half. With no gold, the wages empty the till; if you keep not paying, they leave, the most expensive first. Train what you can afford.",
		"TUT_TIP_CONSUMPTION_TITLE": "People eat",
		"TUT_TIP_CONSUMPTION_BODY": "Each villager eats 1 food per cycle. If it runs short, morale collapses and production with it; below 30 nobody is born. More farms before more houses.",
		"TUT_TIP_AUDIT_TITLE": "The Regency is coming",
		"TUT_TIP_AUDIT_BODY": "That's it: Headquarters at level 3 and the three campaigns won. The Regency launches its Final Assault: 4 to 5 waves in a row against whoever is home, with no training in between. When you are ready, press LET THEM COME in MISSIONS.\n\nLosing does not end the game: it costs dearly, and you can try again.",
